meta {
  name: Export JSON
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/export/json
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-PHI-Shield: off
  ~X-PHI-Unmask-Reason: Investigating%20a%20data%20issue
  ~X-PHI-Unmask-Notes: ticket%20OPP-000
}

body:json {
  {
    "connectionId": "{{connectionId}}",
    "sql": "SELECT 1",
    "defaultLimit": 500
  }
}

docs {
  Run a read-only query and download the masked results as JSON.

  `defaultLimit`: a number caps the rows (at most MAX_ROWS); `null` turns the auto-limit off (up to MAX_ROWS); omitted uses the built-in 500. Ignored when the query sets its own limit.

  503 `CONNECTION_FAILED` when the database can't be reached (D-Pilot never answers 502/504 itself: those mean a proxy couldn't reach D-Pilot).

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability for the connection's environment — 403 otherwise (admins hold every environment).
  Supports PHI unmask headers (disabled by default; enable to reveal PHI where permitted). Reason and notes are URI-encoded (`encodeURIComponent`) free text; the audit log stores them decoded.
}
